    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.comment\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHi there! Would it be possible to implement block commenting, please?\r\nI mean, for now, when you select some lines in visual mode, and press `gc`, all of them goes sommented by single line commentstring on each of that line.\r\n\r\nBut, for example, in https://github.com/numToStr/Comment.nvim you can type `gb` and comment the whole block with block comments, if it is supported (say, `--[[...]]` for Lua, and `/*...*/` for C++, and so on).\r\n\r\n\r\n// By the way, interesting thing: I tried to look in `commentstring` and `comments` while tested both `mini.commentstring` and `Comment` on Lua files, and there was only `--` mentioned there, but somehow `Comment` anyway supports block commentaries syntax :shrug: \r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-06-10T09:57:40Z",
