        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Hi there!\r\n\r\nHello! Thanks for your interest in 'mini.comment'!\r\n\r\n> Would it be possible to implement block commenting, please? I mean, for now, when you select some lines in visual mode, and press `gc`, all of them goes sommented by single line commentstring on each of that line.\r\n> \r\n> But, for example, in https://github.com/numToStr/Comment.nvim you can type `gb` and comment the whole block with block comments, if it is supported (say, `--[[...]]` for Lua, and `/*...*/` for C++, and so on).\r\n\r\nSorry, no. For at least these reasons:\r\n- There is no Neovim's built-in option which would provide information about appropriate block comment structure. Like 'commentstring' is for per-line comments.\r\n- Whole code base of 'mini.comment' is designed for per-line commenting. Adding block comment would mean its complete rewrite, which I don't find necessary yet.\r\n\r\n> // By the way, interesting thing: I tried to look in `commentstring` and `comments` while tested both `mini.commentstring` and `Comment` on Lua files, and there was only `--` mentioned there, but somehow it anyway supports block commentaries syntax shrug\r\n\r\nThis is because 'numToStr/Comment.nvim' [manually stores comment structure for supported filetypes](https://github.com/numToStr/Comment.nvim/blob/c8043290f2d77f61025494d839d88e414608c460/lua/Comment/ft.lua#L16) and *exactly* what is out of scope for 'mini.comment'.",
